  "summary": "Chalk-white clay figurines whistled and painted in bright dots — the spring-fair toy of Vyatka.",
  "description": "Dymkovo toys are molded from local red clay, chalk-whitened and painted in pure geometry: crimson circles, blue dots, golden diamonds over nursemaids, hussars on horses, turkeys with fan tails and whistling water-carriers. Born for the annual spring Svistunya fair — where crowds whistled to honor the fallen of a 1418 battle — the toy became Vyatka's emblem and one of Russia's oldest surviving crafts, still made by hereditary toywomen whose geometric painting pays no regard to anatomy, only to rhythm.",
